    "text": "Gile is an Irish heroine or goddess of Lough Gill. This lake stands beside the city of Sligo in the west. She was the daughter of Romra. While bathing in a spring, Gile saw her lover Omra approach. Ashamed at being seen naked, she ducked her head and drowned. Her foster mother wept so hard that her tears joined the spring to form Lough Gill. Romra and Omra then fought and killed each other. Cairns mark their graves.",
